** MMP9550 - WRITE OPERAND-LIST CONTINUATION FIXTURE, NO COLSPEC TOKEN
** Sibling of MMP9500 (issue 4.11a/#24): that fixture's continuation lines
** each carry a report-writer column-spec token ("5T"/"30T"), which is what
** CONTINUATION_LEAD_COLSPEC keys off. This one wraps the same way but
** without any column-spec token riding along, exercising the three other
** WRITE-scoped continuation leads instead: a line opening with a quoted
** literal (CONTINUATION_LEAD_QUOTE, checked unconditionally -- no verb ever
** starts with a bare literal), a bare "/" skip-a-line marker with nothing
** else on it (CONTINUATION_LEAD_SLASH), and a bare field reference
** (CONTINUATION_LEAD_FIELD, restricted to a leading "#" and excluding a
** ":=" so a genuine bare assignment statement isn't mistaken for another
** WRITE operand). All three are scoped to WRITE/DISPLAY/PRINT/INPUT/
** REINPUT only, same as CONTINUATION_LEAD_COLSPEC.
DEFINE DATA LOCAL
1 #BATCH-SEQ (N4)
1 #BATCH-STATUS (A20)
END-DEFINE
WRITE 'BATCH LOG'
  '- STARTED' #BATCH-SEQ (#BATCH-SEQ + 1)
  /
  #BATCH-STATUS
END
